What is Unmanned Ground Vehicle (UGV)?
Unmanned Ground Vehicles (UGVs) are autonomous or remotely operated robotic systems designed to perform tasks in environments that may be hazardous, high-risk, or inaccessible for human operators. These vehicles integrate advanced technologies such as sensors, artificial intelligence, payload systems, and communication modules to support missions across defense, commercial logistics, mining, and industrial inspection. Because they can navigate complex terrains and execute repetitive or dangerous functions with precision, UGVs have become essential assets in modern defense operations and increasingly in industrial automation.
